## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where remote memory provider calls would reject successful JSON responses when the provider returned a valid decimal `Content-Length` header with leading zeros, such as `00017`.

## Why This Change Was Made

The memory-host SDK bounded JSON response reader now accepts digit-only `Content-Length` values while still rejecting empty, non-decimal, and unsafe integer values. This keeps the fix inside the response-size guard used by `postJson` and batch file upload responses without changing request routing, auth, provider selection, or response body limits.

## User Impact

Remote memory and embedding workflows can parse successful JSON responses from providers that emit leading-zero content lengths, while malformed or oversized responses remain blocked at the same guard boundary.

## Evidence

- Claim proved: `postJson` and `uploadBatchJsonlFile` accept successful JSON responses with leading-zero `Content-Length` headers from a real HTTP response while preserving bounded response parsing.
- Current-head proof at `91b4b4062cbf3f0b85bdc6049a51a604ba5ba0f0`: a repo-local runtime transcript started a localhost HTTP server, returned actual HTTP responses with `Content-Length: 0002` and `Content-Length: 00017`, and called the production SDK entrypoints with Node fetch.

```json
{
  "proof": "real localhost HTTP response with leading-zero Content-Length",
  "postJson": {
    "contentLength": "0002",
    "result": {}
  },
  "uploadBatchJsonlFile": {
    "contentLength": "00017",
    "result": "file_123"
  },
  "serverRequests": [
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "url": "/json",
      "bytes": 13
    },
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "url": "/files",
      "bytes": 365
    }
  ]
}
```

- Focused regression proof: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs packages/memory-host-sdk/src/host/post-json.test.ts packages/memory-host-sdk/src/host/batch-upload.test.ts` passed with 2 shards and 15 tests.
- Diff hygiene: `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` passed.
- Review proof: `python .agents\skills\autoreview\scripts\autoreview --mode branch --base upstream/main` passed with no accepted/actionable findings.
